1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,040
Some ideas are hard to see.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,040
Continuity.

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:09,040
Volumes of revolution.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,040
Quantum spin.

5
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:15,040
Bayes’ theorem.

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:20,029
What if you could test them, level by level?

7
00:00:28,775 --> 00:00:35,815
The university section is built around one idea: model difficult concepts, and learn by testing.

8
00:00:35,875 --> 00:00:44,415
More than ninety games across nine faculties: mathematics, psychology, archaeology, music, economics, law and more.

9
00:00:44,475 --> 00:00:50,815
Change a parameter, make a prediction, and see what the model does.

10
00:00:50,875 --> 00:00:58,673
Then explain it in your own words.

11
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:01,823
Then come the ten main worlds.

12
00:01:01,883 --> 00:01:11,123
Quantum spin, language models, blockchain, game theory, clean energy, genomics, cybersecurity, ecology and the hunt for new planets.

13
00:01:11,183 --> 00:01:19,923
Finish three quarters of the levels in every world with server-verified results, and you earn an achievement card.

14
00:01:19,983 --> 00:01:29,182
Anyone can scan its QR code to check that it’s genuine.

15
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:33,032
In the lecture hall, everyone plays together.

16
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:39,632
Teams join by QR code with just a team name: no accounts, no personal data.

17
00:01:39,692 --> 00:01:48,032
In board mode, the whole hall predicts by a show of hands, and groups take turns at the big screen.

18
00:01:48,092 --> 00:01:55,032
Every solution is recomputed on the server, so the leaderboard counts verified solutions only.

19
00:01:55,092 --> 00:01:59,690
And yes, it gets competitive.

20
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,040
Every week brings a new science mission.

21
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:07,340
One star, TRAPPIST-1, and real catalogue data.

22
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:13,540
How many orbits in a month? How much light is blocked?

23
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:19,540
And just as important: what can the data not tell us?

24
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:30,198
That question is where real research begins.

25
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,048
Being an undergraduate at İDÜ Lab means this:

26
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,048
Difficult ideas become

27
00:02:34,108 --> 00:02:38,048
experiments you can run.

28
00:02:38,108 --> 00:02:46,470
And every skill you master can join your Science Passport as a signed, verifiable badge.

